+The first ingestion downloads the embedding model (BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5, ~130 MB) and caches it.
+Ingestion fails loudly if the model cannot be loaded. To work offline with keyword-only (BM25) retrieval,
+set `RAG_EMBEDDING_BACKEND=none` (PowerShell: `$env:RAG_EMBEDDING_BACKEND="none"`).
+
+After changing the embedding model or switching the backend, re-run ingestion; `docker compose down -v`
+also clears a stale vector store held in the `preauth_data` volume.
+
+---
+
+## Retrieval (RAG)
+
+Policy chunks are embedded locally with fastembed (ONNX, no PyTorch). Each query runs two rankings:
+dense cosine similarity over the embeddings, and BM25 over the text. They are merged with Reciprocal Rank Fusion.
+Hybrid is used because policy text relies on exact identifiers (`Code-Excl02`) that embeddings blur, while
+keyword search misses paraphrases. `clause_lookup` stays an exact match.
+
+| Variable | Default | Purpose |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `RAG_EMBEDDING_BACKEND` | `fastembed` | `none` = BM25 only |
+| `RAG_EMBEDDING_MODEL` | `BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5` | any fastembed text model |
+| `RAG_MIN_SIMILARITY` | `0` | dense hits must score strictly above this |
+| `FASTEMBED_CACHE_PATH` | fastembed default | model cache directory |
+
+`python -m eval.evaluate_rag` reports `retrieval_mode` (`hybrid` or `lexical`) and `avg_expected_passage_recall`.
+
